    "title": "Masters 2026 purse, payouts: How much did Rory McIlroy earn for his second straight win at Augusta National?",
    "text": "Rory McIlroy made history Sunday afternoon at Augusta National, joining yet another elite group of golfers with his latest Masters win.McIlroy, who blew a six-shot lead at the midway point of the tournament, rebounded to grab a one-shot win at the Masters on Sunday afternoon. He is now just the fourth golfer in history to win the green jacket in back-to-back years, joining Jack Nicklaus, Nick Faldo and Tiger Woods.AdvertisementAs a result, McIlroy is also taking home a $4.5 million check.The Masters offered a record $22.5 million purse. While that’s not the largest in the golf world each season, it is the biggest in major event and Masters history.The Masters offered $21 million last year, which earned McIlroy a $4.2 million check to go with his first career green jacket. That was in line with the other three major championships, too. The PGA Championship held a $19 million purse, and the British Open was last at $17 million. The U.S. Open beat the Masters slightly last summer with its $21.5 million purse.The PGA Tour offers signature events with purses of at least $20 million this season, so the Masters is comparable to the Tour’s biggest events. The Players Championship is the richest event of the season, however, with its $25 million purse.AdvertisementHere’s a look at how much McIlroy and the rest of the field earned this week at Augusta National.1. Rory McIlroy — $4.5 million2. Scottie Scheffler — $2.43 millionT3. Tyrrell Hatton, Russell Henley, Justin Rose, Cameron Young — $1.08 millionT7. Collin Morikawa, Sam Burns — $725,625T9. Max Homa, Xander Schauffele — $630,00011. Jake Knapp — $562,500T12. Jordan Spieth, Hideki Matsuyama, Brooks Koepka, Patrick Reed, Patrick Cantlay, Jason Day — $444,167T18. Viktor Hovland, Maverick McNealy, Matt Fitzpatrick — $315,00021. Keegan Bradley, Ludvig Åberg, Wyndham Clark — $252,000T24. Matt McCarty, Adam Scott, Samuel Stevens, Chris Gotterup, Michael Brennan, Brian Campbell, $182,250T30. Alex Noren, Hariss English, Shane Lowry — $146,250T33. Gary Woodland, Dustin Johnson, Brian Harman, Tommy Fleetwood, Ben Griffin — $121,500T38. Jon Rahm, Ryan Gerard, Haotong Li — $101,250T41. Justin Thomas, Sepp Straka, Jacob Bridgeman, Kristoffer Reitan, Nick Taylor — $83,25046. Sungjae Im — $69,75047. Si Woo Kim — $65,25048. Aaron Rai — $61,650T49. Corey Conners, Marco Penge — $57,60051. Kurt Kitayama — $55,35052. Sergio Garcia — $54,00053. Rasmus Højgaard — $52,65054. Charl Schwartzel — $51,300Those who did not make the cut received $25,000 each.",
